# Target: AMD (gfx950) MLA prefill attention (`Attention.mla_prefill` via the
# public `flare_mla_prefill` entry point) -- the DeepSeek/Kimi context-encoding
# op. Targets a deferred-scale online-softmax defect (KERN-2826-class: a
# causally-fully-masked tile reseeds its running max from a stale scaled
# value and double-scales it, overflowing `exp2`). Runtime fuzz axis:
# batch_size, num_keys (== seq_len), and a `spike_mode`/`mu_target_x10` pair
# that engineers the scaled logit `mu = q.k/sqrt(192)` directly, since
# ordinary-magnitude random fills never approach the ~94-99 (or <=-115)
# threshold. num_heads is compile-time (`-D mla_num_heads`, default 16).
# `contract` (finite in -> finite out) is the primary oracle. AMD-only: on
# NVIDIA this entry point compiles to a different (SM100) kernel.
