# Target: MiniMax-M3's 5-way dual-cache fused projection
# (`generic_fused_qkv_index_matmul_kv_cache_paged_ragged_scale_float4`; op
# `mo.fused_qkv_index_matmul.ragged.paged.scale.mxfp8`). One MXFP8 block-scaled
# GEMM over the concatenated weight [Wq|Wk|Wv|Wiq|Wik]: returns Q + IndexQ in a
# combined output, scatters K/V into the MAIN (MHA) paged cache and IndexK into
# the INDEX (MLA, single latent head, K only) paged cache. Bit-exactness vs
# separate matmuls is conditional on every band landing on a 128-elem scale block
# -- the flagged accuracy suspect -- so `ref` (--check 1, host fp32 dequant GEMM)
# verifies BOTH outputs (Q + IndexQ) AND all three cache read-backs (main K, main
# V, index K). The ragged shape (batch, per-batch cache lengths -> scatter slots,
# per-batch new-token counts) is the runtime fuzz axis (M = total tokens);
# head counts/hidden are compile-time (`-D g2_num_q_heads=.. g2_num_kv_heads=..
# g2_num_index_heads=.. g2_hidden=..`, default 8/1/4/256); head_dim fixed at 128.
# memory-safety primary (two cache scatters = OOB-write risk). B200-only.
mojo_test(
    name = "fuzz_fused_qkv_index_matmul_mxfp8.mojo.test",
